<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine cash Jan wheat firm but rains worry.</title>
<headline>Argentine cash Jan wheat firm but rains worry.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine January cash wheat closed firm on the Buenos Aires Cereals exchange on good export buying and downside resistance, but rains in southeast Buenos Aires province began to cause concern, dealers said.</p>
<p>Cash maize trade was quiet. May cash soybeans prices were firm on foreign demand and growing domestic demand, while spot sunflower continued strong on crushers' demand for shipments.</p>
<p>-- Buenos Aires Newsroom, +541 318-0655</p>
</text>
